# The dinner with Strahd in the dining hall (docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_gates.md §5; voice docs/voice/strahd.md).
# He waits at the organ when the party came by his invitation (strahd_invitation == "accepted": the presence
# package's black carriage) and speaks as they come in. He is a host: he feeds them, talks, and leaves. A fight only
# if the party starts one (crg_dinner_affront), and he leaves that too (withdraw). No menu depends on a roll.

~ start
if flag.castle_dinner
-> END
endif
Narrator: The organ stops in the middle of a phrase. The man at the keys closes the lid, gently, and turns on the bench.
quest dinner_at_castle_ravenloft seated
if flag.strahd_first_impression == "defiant"
Strahd [smile]: The guests who told me no across a grave. And here you are at my table. I find that deeply satisfying.
elif flag.strahd_first_impression == "violent"
Strahd [smile]: You drew steel at a funeral. Tonight, I hope, you will settle for the cutlery.
elif flag.strahd_met
Strahd: My guests. You came. Sit, please. I trust the carriage was comfortable.
else
Strahd: Welcome to my house. I am Strahd von Zarovich, and you are very welcome in it.
endif
if guest:ireena
Strahd: Ireena. Candlelight suits you. Sit beside me. No? Then sit wherever you like.
Ireena [angry]: I'll stand.
Strahd: As you wish. The chair will wait. It is good at waiting. So am I.
elif flag.ireena_held_by_strahd
Strahd: Ireena is resting upstairs. She will not join us tonight. It has been a long week for her.
endif
if flag.strahd_test == "fought"
Strahd: We have met on the road, of course. You and my wolves. I have not had a better evening's exercise in years.
endif
if flag.argynvost_beacon_lit
Strahd: Someone lit the old dragon's lamp on the ridge. I watched it from my window. It is very pretty.
endif
if flag.dark_gifts_taken >= 1
Strahd: One of you has been up the mountain, to the temple. I can tell. We have more in common than you would like.
endif
if flag.strahd_knows_marina_truth
Strahd [sad]: I owe you the truth about Marina. I do not often owe anyone. Consider it noted.
endif
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
if quest.the_ladle >= knighted
Strahd: Sir Godrick, of the Order of the Silver Dragon. The last recruit of an order that died in my courtyard. I hope they gave you a good sword. They never had much else.
else
Strahd: And the large young man who calls himself Sir. I have met a great many knights. None of them smiled so much, and none of them lasted.
endif
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Thank you, my lord. I think. Lovely table.
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
Strahd: The little priestess of the dawn. You sing to my windows in the mornings that aren't mornings. I hear everything in my valley. A lovely voice, and a hopeless task.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Morning's grace, my lord. I'll pray for you. No, I insist.
endif
if name:thistle
Strahd: And the wild one. My wolves speak of you. Run with them tonight, after supper, if you like. I will show you a forest no axe has ever touched.
interject name:thistle: No. Your wolves smell wrong. So do you.
endif
if name:wren_featherfoot
if flag.wren_rahadin_met
Strahd: The little monk. My chamberlain tells me you have a teacher's manners. He did not enjoy them. Nobody has unsettled Rahadin in two hundred years.
else
Strahd: A dusk elf taught you to stand like that. I know the stance. I knew a whole people who stood like that.
endif
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Lovely castle. Bit drafty. Bit evil.
endif
if name:kip_smudgewick
if flag.kip_contract_void
Strahd [smile]: And the merchant who paid his devil with my name. I am told your assessor is still furious. I have not laughed so much in a century.
else
Strahd: And a merchant, with ink on his soul. I can smell it from here.
endif
endif
Narrator: Places are laid for each of you. The silver is real, the food is hot, and nobody carries it in.
-> table

~ table
* Why did you invite us? -> why
* Tell us about this house. -> house
* [if guest:ireena or flag.ireena_met] What do you want with Ireena? -> ireena
* [if not flag.crg_dinner_wine_known] [Medicine DC 13] Smell the wine before anyone drinks it. -> wine_ok | wine_fail
* [if not flag.crg_dinner_want_seen] [Insight DC 17] Watch him. What does he actually want? -> want_ok | want_fail
* [if not flag.crg_dinner_grace_said] [Cleric] Say grace before eating. -> grace
* [name:ratatoille] [if not flag.ratatoille_dinner_tasted] Taste the food, critically. -> companions/table:dinner
* [name:kip_smudgewick] [if quest.the_fine_print >= the_small_print and not flag.kip_strahd_signed and not (quest.the_fine_print >= free)] Ask Strahd to sign something. -> companions/fine_print:dinner
* Thank him for his hospitality. -> thanks
* Draw on him. -> affront

~ why
Strahd: Because you are the most interesting thing to happen in my valley for a very long time. And because I wanted to see you up close. Before.
* Before what? -> before
* Fair enough. -> table

~ before
Strahd [smile]: Before whatever you are planning. You are planning something. Everyone who sits at this table is.
-> table

~ house
Strahd: I built it to be seen from everywhere in the valley. I have been looking out of it ever since.
Strahd: Walk where you like tonight. Some doors will open for you and some will not. That is true of every house.
interject class:wizard: Is the library on this floor?
Strahd: Upstairs. I will not say where. Finding it is half the pleasure.
-> table

~ ireena
Strahd: Want? That is a merchant's word. I want nothing from her that she does not choose to give.
if guest:ireena
Ireena [angry]: Then you'll get nothing.
Strahd [smile]: You see? We understand each other already.
else
Strahd: Tell her I asked after her. She will pretend not to care. She always did.
endif
-> table

~ wine_ok
set crg_dinner_wine_known
Narrator: It is wine. Very old, very good, and nothing else at all. He watches you work that out and looks pleased.
Strahd: Poison would be so impolite. And so dull.
-> table

~ wine_fail
Narrator: Plums, cellar dust, and something under them you can't name. Probably only age. Probably.
-> table

~ want_ok
set crg_dinner_want_seen
Narrator: Behind the host's smile is a man who has been bored for centuries. Tonight he is not bored. That is what he wants from you: to stay that way.
-> table

~ want_fail
set crg_dinner_stared
Narrator: You watch him. He watches you watching, smiles, and you learn nothing at all.
Strahd: Do keep looking. I am told I am worth it.
-> table

~ grace
set crg_dinner_grace_said
Narrator: The grace comes out steady. Every candle on the table leans away from the speaker at once, then stands straight again.
Strahd: How brave. Your god has not eaten at this table in a very long time. Do tell him the soup was excellent.
-> table

~ thanks
set castle_dinner = "dined"
quest dinner_at_castle_ravenloft dined
Strahd: You are most welcome. It has been a charming evening. I so rarely get to use the good silver.
if flag.crg_dinner_stared
Strahd [smile]: And you, who watched me all through the meal. I hope you found what you were looking for.
endif
if flag.crg_dinner_want_seen
Strahd: Keep me interested. In this house, it is the only thing that has ever kept anyone safe.
endif
Strahd: The house is yours tonight. Do not let me keep you.
Narrator: He bows, and between one flicker of the candles and the next, the bench at the organ is empty. Somewhere above, a door closes.
-> END

~ affront
set castle_dinner = "affront"
quest dinner_at_castle_ravenloft affront
Narrator: Steel clears the table's edge. A glass goes over. Strahd watches the wine run toward his sleeve, and moves the sleeve.
Strahd: Ah. And the evening was going so well.
combat crg_dinner_affront
